{"accepted_attempt_id":"frontier_attempt_9f1b5541765621498e428f410b375dc9223f67efc08641d531df0802f92ff829","accepted_attempt_index":2,"artifact_role":"frontier_reference","evaluation_only":true,"intuition_id":"frontier_intuition_92ef8d2246b861186ba086704d7a559ca5b26454d6fa1c8f5835dbc86610d0f7","model_visible_theorem_sha256":"49e4f433ffcca8f7087279718474e595d0d053ca0e85facd679bc986bfbf33fd","schema_version":"frontier-intuition-accepted-v1","task_id":"algebra_manipexpr_apbeq2cceqiacpbceqm2","text":"Rewrite \\(a c+b c\\) as \\((a+b)c\\) using distributivity. Substitute \\(a+b=2c\\), then \\(c=i\\), reducing the goal to\n\\[\n(2i)i=-2.\n\\]\nFinish using the defining identity \\(i^2=-1\\) and basic ring normalization. The key intermediate goal is simply \\(c^2=-1\\), obtained from \\(c=i\\).","text_sha256":"84451d932cabb97fb420a58f1be73784251a65e62712f76fad499fa16b21b904","token_count":89,"tokenizer":{"add_special_tokens":false,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base","revision":"49e3418fbbbca6ecbdf9608b4d22e5a407081db4"},"training_eligible":false,"workload":"minif2f-valid-clean-v2"}
